{{2003 Southeastern Conference football standings}}
The '''2003 Georgia Bulldogs football team''' represented the [[University of Georgia]] as a member of the [[Southeastern Conference]] (SEC) during the [[2003 NCAA Division I-A football season]]. Led by third-year head coach [[Mark Richt]], the Bulldogs compiled an overall record of 11–3 with a mark of 6–2 in conference play, sharing the SEC's Eastern Division title with [[2003 Florida Gators football team|Florida]] and [[2003 Tennessee Volunteers football team|Tennessee]]. Georgia advanced to the [[2003 SEC Championship Game|SEC Championship Game]], where the Bulldogs lost to the eventual [[Bowl Championship Series]] (BCS) champion, [[2003 LSU Tigers football team|LSU]]. The Bulldogs finished the season with an overtime win in the [[2004 Capital One Bowl|Capital One Bowl]] over [[2003 Purdue Boilermakers football team|Purdue]]. The team played home games at [[Sanford Stadium]] in [[Athens, Georgia]].

